" just the aggregate base premium, so it remains accurate even with the new block logic.\n- `computePremium`, `roundUpToNearestGold`: Both still fit their behavior.\n- Decision: **Keep all names** — no renaming needed.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (before refactor, the `sumBasePremiums` function body):\n```\nconst counts = new Map<string, number>();       // binding: counts (1)\nfor (const item of items) {                      // loop (5), binding: item (1)\n  counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1); // 2 invocations (set,get)=4, constant 0=1, invocation ??-fallback covered\n}\nlet total = 0;                                    // binding: total (1), constant 0 (1)\nfor (const [type, count] of counts) {             // loop (5), bindings: type, count (2)\n  if (count === 3) {                              // conditional (4), constant 3 (1)\n    total += 60;                                   // assignment (6), constant 60 (1)\n  } else {\n    total += count * BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[type]; // assignment (6), invocation/index (2)\n  }\n}\nreturn total;\n```\nRough total: bindings(1+1+1+2=5) + loops(5+5=10) + invocations(4+2=6) + conditionals(4) + constants(0+3+60=3) + assignments(6+6=12) ≈ **40**\n\n**Rule 3/4 Evaluation (DRY / Fewest Elements)**:\n- Magic numbers `3` (block size) and `60` (block price) were embedded directly in the conditional logic with no explanation of *why* those values matter — this hurts Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) more than it affects mass.\n- No duplication found elsewhere in the file.\n- No unnecessary abstractions to remove.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\nExtracted `BLOCK_SIZE = 3` and `BLOCK_PRICE = 60` as named constants (matching the style already used for `PROCESSING_FEE` and `FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE`), replacing the magic numbers in the conditional branch.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\nSame structural shape — two constant literals (`3`, `60`) became two constant bindings referenced by name instead. Constant count is unchanged (still 2 named values), but they're now bindings instead of anonymous literals, which is neutral for APP mass but a **clarity win** (Rule 2 trumps APP here regardless).\n\nMass Change: ~40 → ~40 (no significant delta — this was a Rule 2 (intent) improvement, not a mass-reduction improvement, which is expected and correct per priority ordering).\n\n**Tests**: All 7 passing tests remain green (verified via `pnpm test`).\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted magic numbers `3` and `60` into named constants `BLOCK_SIZE` and `BLOCK_PRICE` to reveal intent about the \"block of 3 alike items\" business rule.\n**Mass Change**: ~40 → ~40 (intent-focused refactor, not mass-focused; consistent with Rule 2 > APP priority)\n**Tests**: All passing (7/7)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 7\nRecent Green phase: sumBasePremiums rewritten to count items by type using a Map; when count===3 for a type, applies flat 60G block price instead of count*basePremium.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 7\nRecent Green phase: sumBasePremiums rewritten to count items by type using a Map; when count===3 for a type, applies flat 60G block price instead of count*basePremium.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784913279189},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_012Q1DH3E4pDZDCfKCneRS5E","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/quote.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01HQjF18rpm8NEPdGudstEE7","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/quote.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":9959,"output":113,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10072,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784913279209,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-44194773-baee-439e-8e8e-25a7ce3cc9ac","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_012Q1DH3E4pDZDCfKCneRS5E","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { Item, QuoteCustomer } from \"./types.js\";\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n};\n\n// Rounds up to the next whole gold piece, in the MHPCO's favor, while\n// tolerating floating-point representation errors (e.g. 115.00000000000001)\n// that would otherwise incorrectly bump an exact total to the next integer.\nconst roundUpToNearestGold = (amount: number): number => {\n  const correctedAmount = Number(amount.toFixed(6));\n  return Math.ceil(correctedAmount);\n};\n\nconst sumBasePremiums = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of counts) {\n    if (count === 3) {\n      total += 60;\n    } else {\n      total += count * BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[type];\n    }\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nexport const computePremium = (customer: QuoteCustomer, items: Item[]): number => {\n  const policyBase = sumBasePremiums(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance = policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const total = withFirstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return roundUpToNearestGold(total);\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784913281116},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01HQjF18rpm8NEPdGudstEE7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { computePremium } from \"./quote.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Quote - Premium Calculation\", () => {\n  // --- Simplest cases ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, []);\n    expect(result).toBe(5);\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premiums per item type ---\n  it(\"single sword (no modifiers, newcomer) -> base premium 100 G contributes to total\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"sword\" }]);\n    // 100 base + 10 first insurance = 110, + 5 fee = 115\n    expect(result).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet (no modifiers, newcomer) -> base premium 60 G contributes to total\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"amulet\" }]);\n    // 60 base + 6 first insurance = 66, + 5 fee = 71\n    expect(result).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"single staff (no modifiers, newcomer) -> base premium 80 G contributes to total\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"staff\" }]);\n    // 80 base + 8 first insurance = 88, + 5 fee = 93\n    expect(result).toBe(93);\n  });\n  it(\"single potion (no modifiers, newcomer) -> base premium 40 G contributes to total\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"potion\" }]);\n    // 40 base + 4 first insurance = 44, + 5 fee = 49\n    expect(result).toBe(49);\n  });\n\n  // --- Components and building blocks ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> base premium 50 G (25 G each, no block)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    // 50 base + 5 first insurance = 55, + 5 fee = 60\n    expect(result).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> base premium 60 G (block of 3 alike components applies)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    // 60 base (block) + 6 first insurance = 66, + 5 fee = 71\n    expect(result).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"4 runes -> base premium 100 G (no block - block requires exactly 3)\");\n  it.todo(\"7 runes -> base premium 175 G (one block of 3 at 60 G + 4 singles at 25 G each = 60 + 100)\");\n  it.todo(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> base premium 75 G (no block: different types not alike)\");\n  it.todo(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> base premium 120 G (two separate blocks of 60 G each)\");\n\n  // --- Modifier: cursed item surcharge (item-specific) ---\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (base 100 G) -> curse surcharge adds 50 G (50% of item's base premium)\");\n\n  // --- Modifier: high enchantment surcharge (item-specific), thresholds ---\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment exactly 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies (30% of base)\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge applies\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with enchantment exactly 5 -> both curse and high-enchantment surcharges apply\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy with cursed sword (100 G base) + plain amulet (60 G base) -> policy base 160 G, \" +\n      \"curse surcharge +50 G (50% of cursed item's base only) -> 210 G before further modifiers and fee\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Policy-wide modifiers: loyalty discount ---\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO -> loyalty discount (20%) applies to policy base premium\");\n\n  // --- Policy-wide modifiers: first insurance surcharge / follow-up contract discount ---\n  it.todo(\"first quote for a customer -> first insurance surcharge (10%) applies to policy base premium\");\n  it.todo(\"second quote for a customer in a scenario -> follow-up contract discount (15%) applies, \" +\n    \"but first insurance surcharge still applies to each item (per spec clarification)\");\n\n  // --- Processing fee ---\n  it.todo(\"processing fee of 5 G is added at the very end, after all other modifiers\");\n\n  // --- Rounding in the MHPCO's favor ---\n  it.todo(\"premium calculation yielding 197.5 G rounds up to 198 G\");\n\n  // --- Integration examples from spec ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"Newcomer with a cursed sword (steel, enchantment 3), 0 years, no previous contract -> premium 165 G \" +\n      \"(100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance = 160, +5 fee = 165)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"Long-standing customer's second contract: 3 years, second quote in scenario, cursed sword \" +\n      \"(steel, enchantment 7) -> premium 160 G \" +\n      \"(100 base + 50 curse + 30 high enchantment - 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance - 15 follow-up = 155, +5 fee = 160)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Error case: unknown item type ---\n  it.todo(\"quote with an unknown item type (e.g. 'broomstick') -> throws an error\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784913281116},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01UJrwZ2tLUR1dHvR8vP6ssn","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":2834,"output":200,"cacheRead":9957,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12991,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784913281117,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-3911f62d-7479-4c80-8209-f357984a05dc","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResu