Code Mass** (same loop, now delegated to `priceForItemGroup`):\n```ts\nfor (const [type, count] of counts) {\n  total += priceForItemGroup(type, count);\n}\n```\n- Bindings: `type`, `count` = 2\n- Invocation: `priceForItemGroup(...)` × 2 = 2\n- Loop: 1 × 5 = 5\n- Assignment: 1 × 6 = 6\n- Total (loop body) = **15**\n\nThe extracted conditional itself (`priceForItemGroup`) still carries its own mass (ternary conditional = 4, bindings `type`/`count` = 2, invocation into `BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[type]` lookup ~ constant access, multiplication = 2) ≈ 9, but it is now a single-purpose, independently named, testable unit rather than inlined control flow.\n\n- Loop-body mass: 23 -> 15 (delta -8, moved into a well-named helper)\n- Total system mass is roughly unchanged (logic didn't disappear, just relocated), but Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) improved: the pricing rule now has an explicit name and a comment explaining *why* it exists, separate from the mechanics of grouping/summing.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Naming: Kept `sumBasePremiums`, `computePremium`, `roundUpToNearestGold` — all still accurately describe behavior.\n- Extracted `priceForItemGroup(type, count)` from the inline `if/else` inside `sumBasePremiums`'s loop, giving the block-discount business rule its own name and comment.\n- Mass: Loop body mass reduced from 23 to 15 by replacing inline conditional+two assignment branches with a single invocation and single assignment.\n- Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) improved: `sumBasePremiums` now reads as \"group items by type, then price each group\" — the *how* of block pricing is isolated and named, making the loop trivially easy to scan.\n- Rule 3 (DRY): No duplication was found elsewhere in the file to address.\n- Rule 4 (Fewest Elements): The one new function is justified — it turns an anonymous business rule into a documented, reusable, named concept, not speculative abstraction.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `priceForItemGroup` helper from `sumBasePremiums`'s conditional to isolate and name the \"block of 3 alike items\" pricing rule.\n**Mass Change**: Loop body 23 -> 15 (logic relocated into a small, clearly named, documented function rather than eliminated)\n**Tests**: All 10 passing, no regressions"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 10\nRecent Green phase: Added moonstone:25 entry to BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE lookup table. Since sumBasePremiums groups by exact item.type string, runes and moonstones are automatically treated as distinct types (not \"alike\") without any new logic.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 10\nRecent Green phase: Added moonstone:25 entry to BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE lookup table. Since sumBasePremiums groups by exact item.type string, runes and moonstones are automatically treated as distinct types (not \"alike\") without any new logic.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784913411625},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01HnQAGtz4BhCL168vbPyQ1b","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/quote.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_012rLCC57ZGQDM6MbBMsNEe1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/quote.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":243,"output":113,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10112,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784913411645,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-50ade57f-c27f-4550-96e3-926dfa6fc371","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01HnQAGtz4BhCL168vbPyQ1b","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { Item, QuoteCustomer } from \"./types.js\";\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\n// Rounds up to the next whole gold piece, in the MHPCO's favor, while\n// tolerating floating-point representation errors (e.g. 115.00000000000001)\n// that would otherwise incorrectly bump an exact total to the next integer.\nconst roundUpToNearestGold = (amount: number): number => {\n  const correctedAmount = Number(amount.toFixed(6));\n  return Math.ceil(correctedAmount);\n};\n\nconst sumBasePremiums = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of counts) {\n    if (count === BLOCK_SIZE) {\n      total += BLOCK_PRICE;\n    } else {\n      total += count * BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[type];\n    }\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nexport const computePremium = (customer: QuoteCustomer, items: Item[]): number => {\n  const policyBase = sumBasePremiums(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance = policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const total = withFirstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return roundUpToNearestGold(total);\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784913413181},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_012rLCC57ZGQDM6MbBMsNEe1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { computePremium } from \"./quote.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Quote - Premium Calculation\", () => {\n  // --- Simplest cases ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, []);\n    expect(result).toBe(5);\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premiums per item type ---\n  it(\"single sword (no modifiers, newcomer) -> base premium 100 G contributes to total\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"sword\" }]);\n    // 100 base + 10 first insurance = 110, + 5 fee = 115\n    expect(result).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet (no modifiers, newcomer) -> base premium 60 G contributes to total\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"amulet\" }]);\n    // 60 base + 6 first insurance = 66, + 5 fee = 71\n    expect(result).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"single staff (no modifiers, newcomer) -> base premium 80 G contributes to total\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"staff\" }]);\n    // 80 base + 8 first insurance = 88, + 5 fee = 93\n    expect(result).toBe(93);\n  });\n  it(\"single potion (no modifiers, newcomer) -> base premium 40 G contributes to total\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"potion\" }]);\n    // 40 base + 4 first insurance = 44, + 5 fee = 49\n    expect(result).toBe(49);\n  });\n\n  // --- Components and building blocks ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> base premium 50 G (25 G each, no block)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    // 50 base + 5 first insurance = 55, + 5 fee = 60\n    expect(result).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> base premium 60 G (block of 3 alike components applies)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    // 60 base (block) + 6 first insurance = 66, + 5 fee = 71\n    expect(result).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> base premium 100 G (no block - block requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    // 100 base + 10 first insurance = 110, + 5 fee = 115\n    expect(result).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> base premium 175 G (no block - block requires exactly 3 total, not multiples)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    // 175 base (7 * 25, no block) + 17.5 first insurance = 192.5, + 5 fee = 197.5, rounds up to 198\n    expect(result).toBe(198);\n  });\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> base premium 75 G (no block: different types not alike)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ]);\n    // 75 base (2*25 + 1*25, no block since types differ) + 7.5 first insurance = 82.5, + 5 fee = 87.5, rounds up to 88\n    expect(result).toBe(88);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> base premium 120 G (two separate blocks of 60 G each)\");\n\n  // --- Modifier: cursed item surcharge (item-specific) ---\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (base 100 G) -> curse surcharge adds 50 G (50% of item's base premium)\");\n\n  // --- Modifier: high enchantment surcharge (item-specific), thresholds ---\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment exactly 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies (30% of base)\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge applies\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with enchantment exactly 5 -> both curse and high-enchantment surcharges apply\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy with cursed sword (100 G base) + plain amulet (60 G base) -> policy base 160 G, \" +\n      \"curse surcharge +50 G (50% of cursed item's base only) -> 210 G before further modifiers and fee\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Policy-wide modifiers: loyalty discount ---\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO -> loyalty discount (20%) applies to policy base premium\");\n\n  // --- Policy-wide modifiers: first insurance surcharge / follow-up contract discount ---\n  it.todo(\"first quote for a customer -> first insurance surcharge (10%) applies to policy base premium\");\n  it.todo(\"second quote for a customer in a scenario -> follow-up contract discount (15%) applies, \" +\n    \"but first insurance surcharge still applies to each item (per spec clarification)\");\n\n  // --- Processing fee ---\n  it.todo(\"processing fee of 5 G is added at the very end, after all other modifiers\");\n\n  // --- Rounding in the MHPCO's favor ---\n  it.todo(\"premium calculation yielding 197.5 G rounds up to 198 G\");\n\n  // --- Integration examples from spec ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"Newcomer with a cursed sword (steel, enchantment 3), 0 years, no previous contract -> premium 165 G \" +\n      \"(100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance = 160, +5 fee = 165)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"Long-standing customer's second contract: 3 years, second quote in scenario, cursed sword \" +\n      \"(steel, enchantment 7) -> premium 160 G \" +\n      \"(100 base + 50 curse + 30 high enchantment - 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance - 15 follow-up = 155, +5 fee = 160)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Error case: unknown item type ---\n  it.todo(\"quote with an unknown item type (e.g. 'broomstick') -> throws an error\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784913413181},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_016kcdosXRE5K3YKE1D95m1J","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":3339,"output":154,"cacheRead":9997,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13490,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784913413182,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-d1cb3018-4920-48d7-8914-cdf911197889","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_016kcdosXRE5K3YKE1D95m1J","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n\n ✓ src/quote.spec.ts  (24 tests | 14 skipped) 2ms\n ↓ src/claim.spec.ts  (18 tests | 18 skipped)\n ↓ src/cli.spec.ts  (5 tests | 5 skipped)\n\n Test Files  1 passed | 2 skipped (3)\n      Tests  10 passed | 37 todo (47)\n   Start at  17:16:56\n   Duration  406ms (transform 31ms, setup 0ms, collect 45ms, tests 2ms, environment 0ms, prepare 129ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784913416878},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me evaluate the current implementation and apply the refactoring process."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_017M1tAwKUe1JKXZqwyBMP34","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail