items is priced as a discounted\n// bundle (BLOCK_PRICE) instead of at the per-item base premium.\nconst priceForItemGroup = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PRICE : count * getBasePremiumForType(type);\n\nconst sumBasePremiums = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of counts) {\n    total += priceForItemGroup(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst sumItemModifierSurcharges = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => {\n    const itemBase = getBasePremiumForType(item.type);\n    const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? itemBase * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n    const isHighlyEnchanted = (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\n    const enchantmentSurcharge = isHighlyEnchanted ? itemBase * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n    return sum + curseSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n  }, 0);\n\nexport const computePremium = (customer: QuoteCustomer, items: Item[]): number => {\n  const policyBase = sumBasePremiums(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance = policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const withItemSurcharges = withFirstInsurance + sumItemModifierSurcharges(items);\n  const total = withItemSurcharges + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return roundUpToNearestGold(total);\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784914280713},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"File confirmed identical to pre-refactor state, tests still green.\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Naming Evaluation**: `sumItemModifierSurcharges` was checked against its expanded purpose (now handling both curse and high-enchantment surcharges). The name is generic enough to already cover both modifiers accurately. **Decision: Keep current name** — no rename needed.\n\n**Refactoring Attempted**: Extracted the repeated `condition ? itemBase * rate : 0` pattern (present for both curse and enchantment surcharges) into a shared `surchargeWhen(applies, itemBase, rate)` helper to address Rule 3 (DRY).\n\n**Mass Calculation**:\n- Before: 28 (4 constants + 7 bindings + 4 invocations + 8 conditionals + 5 loop = 28)\n- After: 32 (3 constants + 10 bindings + 10 invocations + 4 conditionals + 5 loop = 32)\n- Delta: +4 (worse)\n\n**Decision: Reverted.** The extraction increased mass and required an awkward `Boolean(item.cursed)` cast, while hiding a simple, already-clear ternary behind an extra indirection layer. Per Rule 2 (clarity trumps DRY/APP) and Rule 4 (fewest elements), the abstraction wasn't justified — the two ternaries are conceptually simple, differently-shaped one-liners rather than true duplicated logic worth extracting.\n\n**Reasoning for no net change**: The current `sumItemModifierSurcharges` implementation is already minimal and self-documenting: each surcharge is computed inline with a clearly named boolean condition (`isHighlyEnchanted`) and clearly named intermediate result (`curseSurcharge`, `enchantmentSurcharge`). No unnecessary abstractions exist elsewhere in the file (`getBasePremiumForType`, `priceForItemGroup`, `sumBasePremiums`, `roundUpToNearestGold` all have single, clear responsibilities with good names and comments explaining non-obvious business rules).\n\n**Tests**: All 13 tests passing (confirmed before and after the trial refactor, and after the revert).\n\n**Mass Change**: 28 → 28 (no net change; the one improvement attempt was tried, measured, and reverted because it made things worse)."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":4727,"output":784,"cacheRead":19731,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":25242,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784914280714,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-367a67d4-b3df-4b94-bb3c-ce2d02e23ac4","responseModel":"claude