nDecision: Keep `computePremium`'s name — it fits. Extract the loyalty-discount logic into a named helper `computeLoyaltyDiscount(customer, policyBase)` to match the existing pattern of `sumItemModifierSurcharges`, improving intent-revealing structure (Rule 2) and reducing the main function's local variable count.\n\n## APP Mass Calculation\n\n**Before:**\n```js\nexport const computePremium = (customer, items) => {\n  const policyBase = sumBasePremiums(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance = policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const isLoyalCustomer = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n  const loyaltyDiscount = isLoyalCustomer ? policyBase * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  const withPolicyModifiers = withFirstInsurance - loyaltyDiscount;\n  const withItemSurcharges = withPolicyModifiers + sumItemModifierSurcharges(items);\n  const total = withItemSurcharges + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return roundUpToNearestGold(total);\n};\n```\n- Bindings: customer, items, policyBase, withFirstInsurance, isLoyalCustomer, loyaltyDiscount, withPolicyModifiers, withItemSurcharges, total = 9 → 9\n- Constants: 1, LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD, LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE, FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE, 0, PROCESSING_FEE = 6 → 6\n- Invocations: sumBasePremiums, sumItemModifierSurcharges, roundUpToNearestGold = 3 → 6\n- Conditionals: ternary = 1 → 4\n- Assignments: 0 (all `const`, treated as bindings not mutations) → 0\n\nTotal Mass ≈ 9 + 6 + 6 + 4 = 25\n\n**After:**\n```js\nconst computeLoyaltyDiscount = (customer, policyBase) => {\n  const isLoyalCustomer = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n  return isLoyalCustomer ? policyBase * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n};\n\nexport const computePremium = (customer, items) => {\n  const policyBase = sumBasePremiums(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance = policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const withPolicyModifiers = withFirstInsurance - computeLoyaltyDiscount(customer, policyBase);\n  const withItemSurcharges = withPolicyModifiers + sumItemModifierSurcharges(items);\n  const total = withItemSurcharges + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return roundUpToNearestGold(total);\n};\n```\n- `computeLoyaltyDiscount`: bindings (customer, policyBase, isLoyalCustomer)=3, constants (LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD, LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE, 0)=3, conditional=1(×4=4) → 3+3+4=10\n- `computePremium`: bindings (customer, items, policyBase, withFirstInsurance, withPolicyModifiers, withItemSurcharges, total)=7, constants (1, FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE, PROCESSING_FEE)=3, invocations (sumBasePremiums, computeLoyaltyDiscount, sumItemModifierSurcharges, roundUpToNearestGold)=4(×2=8) → 7+3+8=18\n\nTotal Mass = 10 + 18 = 28\n\nMass Change: 25 → 28 (Δ +3)\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n- **Naming**: Kept `computePremium` (still accurate); introduced `computeLoyaltyDiscount` to name the loyalty-discount concept explicitly, mirroring the existing `sumItemModifierSurcharges` helper.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Improved — `computePremium`'s body now reads as a flat pipeline of named modifier steps, each modifier's internal logic (including its own conditional) is encapsulated behind a descriptive function name instead of being inlined with two extra local variables.\n- **Rule 3 (DRY)**: N/A — no duplication found.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: Mass increased slightly (+3) due to the new function's parameter list and repeated constant references, but Rule 2 (clarity) takes priority over APP mass per the stated guidelines — the extraction makes the main function's structure consistent with its sibling helper and easier to scan.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `computeLoyaltyDiscount(customer, policyBase)` from inline logic in `computePremium`, matching the existing `sumItemModifierSurcharges` pattern.\n**Mass Change**: 25 → 28 (+3, accepted per Rule 2 > APP priority)\n**Tests**: All 17 passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent Green phase: Added LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE=0.2 and LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD=2 constants. computePremium now computes isLoyalCustomer = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2, loyaltyDiscount = isLoyalCustomer ? policyBase*0.2 : 0, and subtracts it from withFirstInsurance before adding item surcharges and the fee.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent Green phase: Added LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE=0.2 and LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD=2 constants. computePremium now computes isLoyalCustomer = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2, loyaltyDiscount = isLoyalCustomer ? policyBase*0.2 : 0, and subtracts it from withFirstInsurance before adding item surcharges and the fee.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784914378962},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_012LcjAwXcPzr59ZXTbTuG26","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/quote.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01V2fpyC41yG7X2MJu5o9Cdr","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/quote.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":10057,"output":113,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10170,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784914378981,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-eaa65d72-c920-44d5-83d0-2f30af68c506","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_012LcjAwXcPzr59ZXTbTuG26","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { Item, QuoteCustomer } from \"./types.js\";\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\n// Rounds up to the next whole gold piece, in the MHPCO's favor, while\n// tolerating floating-point representation errors (e.g. 115.00000000000001)\n// that would otherwise incorrectly bump an exact total to the next integer.\nconst roundUpToNearestGold = (amount: number): number => {\n  const correctedAmount = Number(amount.toFixed(6));\n  return Math.ceil(correctedAmount);\n};\n\nconst getBasePremiumForType = (type: string): number => BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[type];\n\n// A block of exactly BLOCK_SIZE alike items is priced as a discounted\n// bundle (BLOCK_PRICE) instead of at the per-item base premium.\nconst priceForItemGroup = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PRICE : count * getBasePremiumForType(type);\n\nconst sumBasePremiums = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of counts) {\n    total += priceForItemGroup(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst sumItemModifierSurcharges = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => {\n    const itemBase = getBasePremiumForType(item.type);\n    const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? itemBase * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n    const isHighlyEnchanted = (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\n    const enchantmentSurcharge = isHighlyEnchanted ? itemBase * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n    return sum + curseSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n  }, 0);\n\nexport const computePremium = (customer: QuoteCustomer, items: Item[]): number => {\n  const policyBase = sumBasePremiums(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance = policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const isLoyalCustomer = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n  const loyaltyDiscount = isLoyalCustomer ? policyBase * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  const withPolicyModifiers = withFirstInsurance - loyaltyDiscount;\n  const withItemSurcharges = withPolicyModifiers + sumItemModifierSurcharges(items);\n  const total = withItemSurcharges + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return roundUpToNearestGold(total);\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784914380999},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01V2fpyC41yG7X2MJu5o9Cdr","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { computePremium } from \"./quote.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Quote - Premium Calculation\", () => {\n  // --- Simplest cases ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, []);\n    expect(result).toBe(5);\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premiums per item type ---\n  it(\"single sword (no modifiers, newcomer) -> base premium 100 G contributes to total\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"sword\" }]);\n    // 100 base + 10 first insurance = 110, + 5 fee = 115\n    expect(result).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet (no modifiers, newcomer) -> base premium 60 G contributes to total\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"amulet\" }]);\n    // 60 base + 6 first insurance = 66, + 5 fee = 71\n    expect(result).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"single staff (no modifiers, newcomer) -> base premium 80 G contributes to total\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"staff\" }]);\n    // 80 base + 8 first insurance = 88, + 5 fee = 93\n    expect(result).toBe(93);\n  });\n  it(\"single potion (no modifiers, newcomer) -> base premium 40 G contributes to total\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"potion\" }]);\n    // 40 base + 4 first insurance = 44, + 5 fee = 49\n    expect(result).toBe(49);\n  });\n\n  // --- Components and building blocks ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> base premium 50 G (25 G each, no block)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    // 50 base + 5 first insurance = 55, + 5 fee = 60\n    expect(result).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> base premium 60 G (block of 3 alike components applies)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    // 60 base (block) + 6 first insurance = 66, + 5 fee = 71\n    expect(result).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> base premium 100 G (no block - block requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    // 100 base + 10 first insurance = 110, + 5 fee = 115\n    expect(result).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> base premium 175 G (no block - block requires exactly 3 total, not multiples)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    // 175 base (7 * 25, no block) + 17.5 first insurance = 192.5, + 5 fee = 197.5, rounds up to 198\n    expect(result).toBe(198);\n  });\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> base premium 75 G (no block: different types not alike)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ]);\n    // 75 base (2*25 + 1*25, no block since types differ) + 7.5 first insurance = 82.5, + 5 fee = 87.5, rounds up to 88\n    expect(result).toBe(88);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> base premium 120 G (two separate blocks of 60 G each)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ]);\n    // 120 base (60+60, two separate blocks) + 12 first insurance = 132, + 5 fee = 137\n    expect(result).toBe(137);\n  });\n\n  // --- Modifier: cursed item surcharge (item-specific) ---\n  it(\"cursed sword (base 100 G) -> curse surcharge adds 50 G (50% of item's base premium)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"sword\", cursed: true },\n    ]);\n    // policy base 100, + 10 first insurance (10% of 100) = 110, + 50 curse surcharge = 160, + 5 fee = 165\n    expect(result).toBe(165);\n  });\n\n  // --- Modifier: high enchantment surcharge (item-specific), thresholds ---\n  it(\"sword with enchantment exactly 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies (30% of base)\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 },\n    ]);\n    // policy base 100, + 10 first insurance = 110, + 30 high-enchantment surcharge = 140, + 5 fee = 145\n    expect(result).toBe(145);\n  });\n  it(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge applies\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4 },\n    ]);\n    // policy base 100, + 10 first insurance = 110, no surcharge, + 5 fee = 115\n    expect(result).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"cursed sword with enchantment exactly 5 -> both curse and high-enchantment surcharges apply\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n      { type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true },\n    ]);\n    // policy base 100, + 10 first insurance = 110, + 50 curse + 30 enchantment = 190, + 5 fee = 195\n    expect(result).toBe(195);\n  });\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it(\n    \"policy with cursed sword (100 G base) + plain amulet (60 G base) -> policy base 160 G, \" +\n      \"curse surcharge +50 G (50% of cursed item's base only) -> 210 G before further modifiers and fee\",\n    () => {\n      const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }, [\n        { type: \"sword\", cursed: true },\n        { type: \"amulet\" },\n      ]);\n      // policy base 160 (100+60), + 16 first insurance (10% of 160) = 176, + 50 curse = 226, + 5 fee = 231\n      expect(result).toBe(231);\n    }\n  );\n\n  // --- Policy-wide modifiers: loyalty discount ---\n  it(\"customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO -> loyalty discount (20%) applies to policy base premium\", () => {\n    const result = computePremium({ yearsWithMHPCO: 2, isFollowUpContract: false }, [{ type: \"sword\" }]);\n    // policy base 100, + 10 first insurance = 110, - 20 loyalty (20% of 100) = 90, + 5 fee = 95\n    expect(result).toBe(95);\n  });\n\n  // --- Policy-wide modifiers: first insurance surcharge / follow-up contract discount ---\n  it.todo(\"first quote