ility home for upcoming per-damage rules (dragon-material clause, unknown item type errors, negative amount errors) that the test list already anticipates.\n- **Rule 3 (DRY)**: No duplication found — `findPolicyItem` and `computeReimbursement` are already appropriately separated single-purpose helpers.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: The new function is justified by Rule 2 (clarity) rather than being arbitrary — not adding unnecessary abstraction, since the extracted concept is a distinct, nameable unit of domain logic.\n- **APP Mass**: 25 -> 29 (+4). Mass increased slightly due to the new function's own parameter bindings, but per the guideline \"Rule 2 trumps APP,\" clarity gains (a clearly named `computeDamagePayout` concept) justify the small mass increase.\n\n## Report Completion\n\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `computeDamagePayout(policyItems, damage)` from the inline reduce callback in `computeClaim`, giving the \"single damage → payout\" concept an explicit name.\n**Mass Change**: ≈25 -> ≈29 (+4, accepted per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 28 tests passing (4 in claim.spec.ts, 24 in quote.spec.ts, cli.spec.ts skipped as before)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim.ts\nPassing tests: 4 (in claim.spec.ts; 28 total across project)\nRecent Green phase: Added findPolicyItem(policyItems, itemType) to look up the insured item by type, and computeReimbursement(item, amount) that returns amount*0.5 if item.enchantment >= 8, else amount unchanged. computeClaim now looks up the item per damage, computes reimbursement, then subtracts DEDUCTIBLE.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","con