:"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01TG8Lqra3jF1DmbtV5mrWYf","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 38 tests still pass.\n\n## Naming Evaluation\n\n- Current name: `computeClaim`\n- Function purpose: \"validates damages against policy, sums per-damage payouts, clamps to remaining cap, returns payout and updated remaining cap\"\n- Question: Does `computeClaim` clearly reveal this intent?\n- Assessment: Yes — it's the public orchestration function; \"claim\" appropriately covers the whole validate→sum→clamp flow. It doesn't need to expose the clamping mechanics in its name (that's an implementation detail).\n- Decision: **Keep current name** — it fits.\n\nAlso checked `computeDamagePayout`, `validateDamagesAgainstPolicy`, `computeInsuranceSum`/`computeInsuranceCap` — all still accurately describe their single responsibilities after the cap-clamping addition. No renames needed there either.\n\n## Current Code Mass (before refactor)\n\n```ts\nexport const computeClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  currentRemainingCap: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  validateDamagesAgainstPolicy(policyItems, damages);\n  const desiredPayout = damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + computeDamagePayout(policyItems, damage),\n    0\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(desiredPayout, currentRemainingCap);\n  return { payout, remainingCap: currentRemainingCap - payout };\n};\n```\n\n- Constants: 1 (`0`) = 1\n- Bindings: 6 (`policyItems`, `damages`, `currentRemainingCap`, `desiredPayout`, `payout`, `sum`/`damage` counted together as reduce params ×2) → precisely: `policyItems`, `damages`, `currentRemainingCap`, `desiredPayout`, `payout`, `sum`, `damage` = 7\n- Invocations: 4 (`validateDamagesAgainstPolicy`, `reduce`, `computeDamagePayout`, `Math.min`) = 8\n- Conditionals: 0 = 0\n- Loops: 1 (`reduce`) = 5\n- Assignments: 0 = 0\n\n**Total Mass: 1 + 7 + 8 + 0 + 5 + 0 = 21**\n\n## Applying Simple Design Rules\n\n- **Rule 1 (Tests Pass)**: All 38 tests green before starting. ✅\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: `computeClaim` mixes three concerns inline at the same nesting level: validation, summing desired payout (via an inline `reduce`), and cap-clamping. The inline reduce doesn't carry a name of its own — a reader has to parse the lambda to learn it's \"the payout before capping.\" Extracting it into a named `computeDesiredPayout` helper makes `computeClaim` read as a flat sequence of named steps (validate → desired payout → clamp → result), matching the pattern already used elsewhere in the file (`computeInsuranceSum`, `computeReimbursement`, etc.) and in `quote.ts` (`sumBasePremiums`). This is a clarity win independent of mass.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: No duplicated logic found; `computeDamagePayout` is already a shared, reused unit.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: The new helper adds one top-level function, but it removes an anonymous inline lambda and gives it a name — net neutral on essential complexity, and it improves scannability of `computeClaim`.\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n- Extracted the inline `damages.reduce(...)` computation into a new named function `computeDesiredPayout(policyItems, damages)`, mirroring the existing `computeInsuranceSum` pattern in the same file.\n- `computeClaim` now reads as a clean four-step sequence: validate → compute desired payout → clamp to cap → build result.\n\n## Refactored Code Mass\n\n```ts\nconst computeDesiredPayout = (policyItems: Item[], damages: Damage[]): number =>\n  damages.reduce((sum, damage) => sum + computeDamagePayout(policyItems, damage), 0);\n\nexport const computeClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  currentRemainingCap: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  validateDamagesAgainstPolicy(policyItems, damages);\n  const desiredPayout = computeDesiredPayout(policyItems, damages);\n  const payout = Math.min(desiredPayout, currentRemainingCap);\n  return { payout, remainingCap: currentRemainingCap - payout };\n};\n```\n\n`computeDesiredPayout`: constants 1, bindings 4 (`policyItems`, `damages`, `sum`, `damage`), invocations 2 (`reduce`, `computeDamagePayout`)=4, loops 1=5 → mass 14\n`computeClaim`: bindings 3 (`policyItems`, `damages`, `currentRemainingCap`) + 2 (`desiredPayout`, `payout`) = 5, invocations 3 (`validateDamagesAgainstPolicy`, `computeDesiredPayout`, `Math.min`) = 6 → mass 11\n\n**Total Mass: 14 + 11 = 25** (was 21, delta +4)\n\nMass increased slightly (the extracted function's own signature bindings are now counted separately), but Rule 2 (clarity) takes priority over APP per the guidelines — the resulting `computeClaim` is now a flat, self-documenting sequence of named steps consistent with the file's existing style.\n\n---\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Extracted inline `reduce` in `computeClaim` into a named `computeDesiredPayout` helper, matching the existing `computeInsuranceSum` naming/extraction pattern in the file.\n**Mass Change**: 21 -> 25 (+4, accepted per Rule 2 > APP priority — clarity of `computeClaim`'s step sequence outweighs the small mass increase)\n**Tests**: All 38 passing (18 in claim.spec.ts, 4 still todo/skipped as before)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim.ts\nPassing tests: 14 (in claim.spec.ts; 38 total across project)\nRecent Green phase: computeClaim now computes desiredPayout (sum of computeDamagePayout across damages), then clamps it via payout = Math.min(desiredPayout, currentRemainingCap), and returns remainingCap = currentRemainingCap - payout.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim.ts\nPassing tests: 14 (in claim.spec.ts; 38 total across project)\nRecent Green phase: computeClaim now computes desiredPayout (sum of computeDamagePayout across damages), then clamps it via payout = Math.min(desiredPayout, currentRemainingCap), and returns remainingCap = currentRemainingCap - payout.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784916165552},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01NSBsqCzzk93nak5Z59pCLa","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_013GURivSBxoZjiByJgTGUzq","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":253,"output":119,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10128,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784916165572,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-6d818429-09ab-4b9a-8a16-28b8e7c4cadc","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01NSBsqCzzk93nak5Z59pCLa","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { Item, Damage, ClaimResult } from \"./types.js\";\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 8;\n\nconst findPolicyItem = (policyItems: Item[], itemType: string): Item | undefined =>\n  policyItems.find((item) => item.type === itemType);\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUE_BY_ITEM_TYPE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\n// Named to match the domain language used in the policy spec (\"insurance\n// sum\" vs. \"cap\"), mirroring how quote.ts separates sumBasePremiums from\n// the surcharges/discounts applied on top of it.\nconst computeInsuranceSum = (policyItems: Item[]): number =>\n  policyItems.reduce((sum, item) => sum + INSURANCE_VALUE_BY_ITEM_TYPE[item.type], 0);\n\nexport const computeInsuranceCap = (policyItems: Item[]): number =>\n  computeInsuranceSum(policyItems) * CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst validateDamagesAgainstPolicy = (policyItems: Item[], damages: Damage[]): void => {\n  const remainingByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of policyItems) {\n    remainingByType.set(item.type, (remainingByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  for (const damage of damages) {\n    const remaining = remainingByType.get(damage.itemType) ?? 0;\n    if (remaining <= 0) {\n      throw new Error(`Damage references item type \"${damage.itemType}\" not covered by the policy`);\n    }\n    remainingByType.set(damage.itemType, remaining - 1);\n  }\n};\n\nconst computeReimbursement = (enchantment: number | undefined, amount: number): number => {\n  if ((enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    return amount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return amount;\n};\n\nconst computeDamagePayout = (policyItems: Item[], damage: Damage): number => {\n  const item = findPolicyItem(policyItems, damage.itemType);\n  const reimbursed = computeReimbursement(item?.enchantment, damage.amount);\n  return reimbursed - DEDUCTIBLE;\n};\n\nexport const computeClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  currentRemainingCap: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  validateDamagesAgainstPolicy(policyItems, damages);\n  const desiredPayout = damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + computeDamagePayout(policyItems, damage),\n    0\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(desiredPayout, currentRemainingCap);\n  return { payout, remainingCap: currentRemainingCap - payout };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784916167181},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_013GURivSBxoZjiByJgTGUzq","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { computeClaim, computeInsuranceCap } from \"./claim.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim - Payout Calculation\", () => {\n  // --- Standard reimbursement (no special clauses) ---\n  it(\n    \"regular sword (steel, enchantment 3), damage 500 G -> payout 400 G \" +\n      \"(full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible; no special clause applies)\",\n    () => {\n      const result = computeClaim(\n        [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }],\n        [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }],\n        2000\n      );\n      expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n    }\n  );\n  it(\n    \"damage to a rune (insurance value 250 G), damage 200 G -> payout 100 G \" +\n      \"(full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible; runes have no enchantment level or material)\",\n    () => {\n      const result = computeClaim([{ type: \"rune\" }], [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }], 500);\n      expect(result.payout).toBe(100);\n    }\n  );\n\n  // --- Deductible per damage event ---\n  it(\n    \"dragon attack damages an insured sword (500 G) and an insured amulet (300 G) -> payout 600 G \" +\n      \"(100 G deductible applies once per damaged item)\",\n    () => {\n      const result = computeClaim(\n        [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }],\n        [\n          { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n          { itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 300 },\n        ],\n        3200\n      );\n      expect(result.payout).toBe(600);\n    }\n  );\n\n  // --- High enchantment clause (>= 8) ---\n  it(\n    \"steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G \" +\n      \"(only high-enchantment clause applies: 50% first, then deductible: 500 - 100)\",\n    () => {\n      const result = computeClaim(\n        [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 9 }],\n        [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n        2000\n      );\n      expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n    }\n  );\n\n  // --- Dragon material clause ---\n  it(\n    \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G -> payout 700 G \" +\n      \"(only dragon-material clause applies: full reimbursement, then deductible: 800 - 100)\",\n    () => {\n      const result = computeClaim(\n        [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5 }],\n        [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }],\n        2000\n      );\n      expect(result.payout).toBe(700);\n    }\n  );\n\n  // --- Both clauses together (dragon-material wins) ---\n  it(\n    \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G \" +\n      \"(both clauses apply; 50% rule wins, then deductible: 500 - 100)\",\n    () => {\n      const result = computeClaim(\n        [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 9 }],\n        [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n        2000\n      );\n      expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n    }\n  );\n  it(\n    \"dragon-material sword with exactly enchantment 8, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G \" +\n      \"(high-enchantment clause applies at exact threshold, then deductible)\",\n    () => {\n      const result = computeClaim(\n        [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 8 }],\n        [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n        2000\n      );\n      expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n    }\n  );\n\n  // --- Multiple items of the same type ---\n  it(\n    \"policy covers two swords, dragon attack damages both (two separate {itemType: 'sword'} damage entries) \" +\n      \"-> each entry treated as a separate damage with its own deductible\",\n    () => {\n      const result = computeClaim(\n        [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"sword\" }],\n        [\n          { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n          { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 300 },\n        ],\n        4000\n      );\n      // (500-100) + (300-100) = 400 + 200 = 600\n      expect(result.payout).toBe(600);\n    }\n  );\n  it(\n    \"damages array contains more entries of a given type than the policy covers \" +\n      \"(e.g. two sword damages but only one sword insured) -> throws an error\",\n    () => {\n      expect(() =>\n        computeClaim(\n          [{ type: \"sword\" }],\n          [\n            { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n            { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 300 },\n          ],\n          2000\n        )\n      ).toThrow();\n    }\n  );\n\n  // --- Cap exhaustion ---\n  it(\"policy covers a sword and an amulet -> insurance sum 1600 G (1000+600), cap 3200 G\", () => {\n    const cap = computeInsuranceCap([{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }]);\n    expect(cap).toBe(3200);\n  });\n  it(\n    \"cursed sword (insurance value 1000 G, premium with modifiers 165 G) -> cap 2000 G \" +\n      \"(based on unmodified insurance value; premium modifiers do not raise the cap)\",\n    () => {\n      const cap = computeInsuranceCap([{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }]);\n      expect(cap).toBe(2000);\n    }\n  );\n  it(\n    \"policy covers a sword and 3 runes (a block) -> insurance sum 1750 G (1000 + 3x250); \" +\n      \"block discount affects premium only, not insurance sum\",\n    () => {\n      const cap = computeInsuranceCap([\n        { type: \"sword\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"rune\" },\n      ]);\n      // insurance sum 1750, cap 3500\n      expect(cap).toBe(3500);\n    }\n  );\n  it(\n    \"sword insured (insurance sum 1000 G, cap 2000 G); two successive claims of 1500 G each: \" +\n      \"first claim -> payout 1400 G, cap remaining 600 G\",\n    () => {\n      const result = computeClaim([{ type: \"sword\" }], [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }], 2000);\n      // desired payout: 1500 - 100 = 1400; within cap 2000, so full amount applies\n      expect(result.payout).toBe(1400);\n      expect(result.remainingCap).toBe(600);\n    }\n  );\n  it(\n    \"sword insured (insurance sum 1000 G, cap 2000 G); two successive claims of 1500 G each: \" +\n      \"second claim -> payout 600 G, cap remaining 0 G (desired 1400 G reduced to remaining cap)\",\n    () => {\n      // After the first claim, remaining cap is 600 G. Desired payout is again 1400 G,\n      // but must be clamped to the 600 G remaining on the cap.\n      const result = computeClaim([{ type: \"sword\" }], [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }], 600);\n      expect(result.payout).toBe(600);\n      expect(result.remainingCap).toBe(0);\n    }\n  );\n\n  // --- Rounding in the MHPCO's favor ---\n  it.todo(\"payout calculation yielding 350.5 G rounds down to 350 G\");\n\n  // --- Error cases ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"claim references a damage entry whose item is not part of the policy \" +\n      \"(e.g. an amulet damaged when only a sword is insured) -> throws an error\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"claim references a damage entry with an unknown item type -> throws an error\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\"claim contains a damage entry with amount: -200 -> throws an error\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784916167181},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Ls9cxjSJojoKTeTL43PZGX","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && cat src/types.ts 2>/dev/null; echo \"---\"; pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":4242,"output":177,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14175,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784916167181,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-2d857a0f-b2b7-4eaa-8b65-ce2d3361a602","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Ls9cxjSJojoKTeTL43PZGX","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteCustomer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n  isFollowUpContract: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n---\n\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n\n ✓ src/quote.spec.ts  (24 tests) 4ms\n ✓ src/claim.spec.ts  (18 tests | 4 skipped) 3ms\n ↓ src/cli.spec.ts  (5 tests | 5 skipped)\n\n Test Files  2 passed | 1 skipped (3)\n      Tests  38 passed | 9 todo (47)\n   Start at  18:02:51\n   Duration  401ms (transform 42ms, setup 0ms, collect 48ms, tests 7ms, environment 0ms, prepare 122ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784916171553},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Hyioivc2CpNjXkoSzPonRA","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/quote.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":4894,"output":1328,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":15978,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784916171553,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-d7e3cb8c-2aad-4d96-a964-96c97e1ba85f","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Hyioivc2CpNjXkoSzPonRA","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { Item, QuoteCustomer } from \"./types.js\";\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\n// Rounds up to the next whole gold piece, in the MHPCO's favor, while\n// tolerating floating-point representation errors (e.g. 115.00000000000001)\n// that would otherwise incorrectly bump an exact total to the next integer.\nconst roundUpToNearestGold = (amount: number): number => {\n  const correctedAmount = Number(amount.toFixed(6));\n  return Math.ceil(correctedAmount);\n};\n\nconst getBasePremiumForType = (type: string): number => {\n  const basePremium = BASE_PREMIUM_BY_ITEM_TYPE[type];\n  if (basePremium === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${type}`);\n  }\n  return basePremium;\n};\n\n// A block of exactly BLOCK_SIZE alike items is priced as a discounted\n// bundle (BLOCK_PRICE) instead of at the per-item base premium.\nconst priceForItemGroup = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PRICE : count * getBasePremiumForType(type);\n\nconst sumBasePremiums = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of counts) {\n    total += priceForItemGroup(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\n// Every surcharge and discount in this policy takes the same shape: a\n// percentage of some base amount, applied only when a condition holds\n// (cursed, highly enchanted, loyal, follow-up contract). Naming that\n// shared shape once avoids repeating \"condition ? base * rate : 0\" for\n// each of the four modifiers below.\nconst amountIfEligible = (condition: boolean | undefined, base: number, rate: number): number =>\n  condition ? base * rate : 0;\n\nconst sumItemModifierSurcharges = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => {\n    const itemBase = getBasePremiumForType(item.type);\n    const curseSurcharge = amountIfEligible(item.cursed, itemBase, CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n    const isHighlyEnchanted = (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\n    const enchantmentSurcharge = amountIfEligible(isHighlyEnchanted, itemBase, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n    return sum + curseSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n  }, 0);\n\n// A returning customer (>= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD years) gets a discount\n// off the policy base premium, mirroring how sumItemModifierSurcharges\n// isolates the item-specific modifiers.\nconst computeLoyaltyDiscount = (customer: QuoteCustomer, policyBase: number): number =>\n  amountIfEligible(customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD, policyBase, LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE);\n\n// A customer on a follow-up contract gets a discount off the policy base\n// premium, mirroring computeLoyaltyDiscount's shape for policy-wide discounts.\nconst computeFollowUpDiscount = (customer: QuoteCustomer, policyBase: number): number =>\n  amountIfEligible(customer.isFollowUpContract, policyBase, FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_DISCOUNT_RATE);\n\nexport const computePremium = (customer: QuoteCustomer, items: Item[]): number => {\n  const policyBase = sumBasePremiums(items);\n  const withFirstInsurance = policyBase * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const loyaltyDiscount = computeLoyaltyDiscount(customer, policyBase);\n  const followUpDiscount = computeFollowUpDiscount(customer, policyBase);\n  const withPolicyModifiers = withFirstInsurance - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount;\n  const withItemSurcharges = withPolicyModifiers + sumItemModifierSurcharges(items);\n  const total = withItemSurcharges + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return roundUpToNearestGold(total);\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784916185176},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_0167JnHiAT3QwfLtupNRRSX9","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-28-54_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && grep -rn \"claim\" src/cli.ts 2>/dev/null; grep -rln \"computeClaim\\|computeInsuranceCap\" src --include=\"*.ts\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":6597,"output":2824,"cacheRead":10007,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":19428,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784916185178,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-31764437-2b65-4a5c-97b4-26ac2ec0f6bc","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_0167JnHiAT3QwfLtupNRRSX9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"src/claim.ts\nsrc/claim.spec.ts\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784916215829},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_015XGokJpjHsfM9Q1ZYqkA8c","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"export const computeClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  currentRemainingCap: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  validateDamagesAgainstPolicy(policyItems, damages);\n  const desiredPayout = damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + computeDamagePayout(policyItems, damage),\n    0\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(desiredPayout, currentRemainingCap);\n  return { payout, remainingCap: currentRemainingCap - payout };\n};","newText":"// Named and extracted to mirror computeInsuranceSum's shape (reduce over\n// policy items to a single total), keeping computeClaim itself a plain\n// sequence of named steps rather than mixing an inline reduce with the\n// cap-clamping logic.\nconst computeDesiredPayout = (policyItems: Item[], damages: Damage[]): number =>\n  damages.reduce((sum, damage) => sum + computeDamagePayout(policyItems, damage), 0);\n\nexport const computeClaim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  currentRemainingCap: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  validateDamagesAgainstPolicy(policyItems, damages);\n  const desiredPayout = computeDesiredPayout(policyItems, damages);\n  const payout = Math.min(desiredPayout, currentRemainingCap);\n  return { payout, remainingCap: currentRemainingCap - payout };\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":6789,"output":3948,"cacheRead":10007,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":20744,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784916215831,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-5a0435c6-422a-45b1-a59a-1cd6c5a9a104","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_015XGokJpjHsfM9Q1ZYqkA8c","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in src/claim.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"    ...\n 53   const reimbursed = computeReimbursement(item?.enchantment, damage.amount);\n 54   return reimbursed - DEDUCTIBLE;\n 55 };\n 56 \n+57 // Named and extracted to mirror computeInsuranceSum's shape (reduce over\n+58 // policy items to a single total), keeping computeClaim itself a plain\n+59 // sequence of named steps rather than mixing an inline reduce with the\n+60 // cap-clamping logic.\n+61 const computeDesiredPayout = (policyItems: Item[], damages: Damage[]): number =>\n+62   damages.reduce((sum, damage) => sum + computeDamagePayout(policyItems, damage), 0);\n+63 \n 57 export const computeClaim = (\n 58   policyItems: Item[],\n 59   damages: Damage[],\n 60   currentRemainingCap: number\n 61 ): ClaimResult => {\n 62   validateDamagesAgainstPolicy(policyItems, damages);\n-63   const desiredPayout = damages.reduce(\n-64     (sum, damage) => sum + computeDamagePayout(policyItems, damage),\n-65     0\n-66   );\n+70   const desiredPayout = computeDesiredPayout(policyItems, damages);\n 67   const payout = Math.min(desiredPayout, currentRemainingCap);\n 68   return { payout, remainingCap: currentRemainingCap - payout };\n 69 };","patch":"--- src/claim.ts\n+++ src/claim.ts\n@@ -53,17 +53,21 @@\n  